Card numbers can exceed `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER`, so you add them as digit strings. What does `addStrings('999', '1')` return with this implementation?

```js
function addStrings(a, b) {
  let i = a.length - 1, j = b.length - 1, carry = 0, out = '';
  while (i >= 0 || j >= 0) {
    const sum = (Number(a[i]) || 0) + (Number(b[j]) || 0) + carry;
    out = (sum % 10) + out;
    carry = Math.floor(sum / 10);
    i--; j--;
  }
  return out;
}
```

